    "raw": "Build an unsupervised pipeline (not IDF/BM25, not supervised ST fine-tuning) that reads our documents and todo text, embeds chunks with sentence-transformers (or compatible dense embedder), and derives terms/phrases that are semantically important in vector space for our domain.\n\nContext from design discussion:\n- Hash embedder and lexical boosts are insufficient for semantic vocabulary discovery.\n- sentence-transformers encode() is the engine only; importance scoring is our pipeline.\n- NOT Apple Create ML / NLContextualEmbedding.\n- NOT document-frequency IDF scores; importance means discriminative/salient in embedding geometry (e.g. term vectors aligned with doc/cluster centroids and far from global corpus centroid; KeyBERT-style doc-term cosine; cluster representatives after UMAP/HDBSCAN).\n\nRelates to todo-embedding branch (sqlite + search) but this ticket is the separate semantic vocabulary layer: corpus ingest, candidate phrase mining, embed, score, persist term table, expose via todo.py (e.g. terms list / terms for doc / search boost hook).\n\nStart after or alongside merging todo-embedding sqlite storage.\n\n--- Curated tags -> embedding phrases (concept; NOT fleshed out here) ---\nA curated tag names a bucket that expands to a list of embedding phrases, e.g.\n  code-health -> [\"test\", \"pytest\", \"iamlazy test\", \"playwright mcp\", ...]\nAuto-tagging matches a todo against these phrase lists (cosine) to assign tags.\nEmpirical note: an unspecialized general embedder (Apple NLCE) does NOT cleanly\nrank such phrases -- compressed cosine range, keys on shared surface tokens over\nconcept (e.g. \"technical debt\" / \"software quality\" score BELOW distractors vs a\n\"code health\" anchor). Motivates the domain-tuned importance pipeline above, not\na raw general embedder. Stop here for now.\n\n--- Planned subtodo (subtask of this ticket): manual `todo tag` mechanism ---\nSeeds the tag corpus, which starts EMPTY. Implementing agent wires the spawn +\nwait-and-merge workitems; NOT spawned here.\n`todo tag <id> <tag>*`:\n- Manually add one or more tags to a todo. Additive; manual tags are NEVER\n  auto-deleted.\n- Tags surfaced in display: shown in `ls` and `search` output.\n- Tags found by search: auto AND manual tags are embedded and become a THIRD\n  cosine match target (alongside the Summary and Body vectors).\n- Out of scope (later): grooming/bucketing tags and deriving the curated\n  tag -> phrase lists that auto-tag todos.\n- Manual tags are retained as regression backstops for the next tagging-training\n  phase."
  },
